namespace LingGuangV05.CaseMenu
{
    public static partial class PlayerKnowledgeCopy
    {
        public static string Summary4(bool english) => english ? "Although your teaching in the game does not directly update the built-in local language model's parameters, the process still has meaning. Set in 2016, the game condenses selected ideas from neural networks and language models into six growth stages. Through practice, trial and error, and feedback, you can explore what different learning methods can solve and where they fall short.\n\nThe stages are: Simple decisions → Combining features → Building specialties → Retaining information → Finding what matters → Reshaping how it learns. They serve the game's experience. They are not a strict timeline of inventions or six steps that every real model must follow." : "尽管玩家在游戏中的训练，并不会直接更新内置本地语言模型的参数，但这一培养过程仍然有意义。本作以 2016 年为故事背景，将神经网络与语言模型发展中的部分重要思路，浓缩为六个成长阶段，让玩家在操作、试错和观察反馈的过程中，直观理解不同学习方法能够解决什么问题，又存在哪些局限。\n\n六个阶段依次是：简单判断 → 组合特征 → 走向专长 → 保留信息 → 寻找重点 → 重构学习方式。它们是服务于游戏体验的能力划分，并不严格对应技术发明的年代顺序，也不代表现实中的模型必须依次经历这六步。";
        public static string Title4(bool english) => english ? "What do the six growth stages mean?" : "六个成长阶段在讲什么？";
        public static string Body4(bool english) => english ? "Stage 1: Simple decisions — starting with yes and no\n\nIt uses limited clues to make simple decisions. By offering examples and correcting answers, you begin a teaching relationship and discover that some problems cannot be separated by one simple rule.\n\nStage 2: Combining features — looking at several clues together\n\nIt starts combining multiple features to tackle more complex classification problems. You need to consider not only how much data it has, but which clues matter and how they work together.\n\nStage 3: Building specialties — learning to handle images and text\n\nVisual and language tasks begin to open up. It uses existing data such as handwritten digits and encounters tasks involving captchas, images and text sequences, moving from simple choices toward word output. Different tasks need different approaches; one method for every problem begins to reach its limits.\n\nStage 4: Retaining information — letting earlier content affect later replies\n\nIt begins handling longer information and trying short sentences. Instead of responding only to one word, it starts using recent conversation history. Producing a word gradually becomes responding to your sentence. Recently saved messages may still be supplied as context across days or after loading a save. This differs from Stage 5, which retrieves relevant information from longer-term records.\n\nStage 5: Finding what matters — locating relevant clues in more information\n\nWith longer sentences and more records, it needs to find what relates to the current question. Translation and conversations across time gradually open up. You start asking whether it found the right evidence, not just whether its answer sounds fluent.\n\nStage 6: Reshaping how it learns — moving toward broader tasks\n\nInspired by ideas such as the Transformer, the game enters a new phase of architecture and scale. It can attempt a wider range of language tasks, bringing new questions: where is it reliable, where does it still fail, and is it ready for others to use?\n\nAcross the first four stages, the central question is whether it can learn. In the last two, the question shifts toward what it will become. Being able to communicate is a milestone. Understanding, testing and responding to its abilities are the questions the later game leaves with you.\n\nReading boundaries: Attention and long-term memory in Stage 5 are different mechanisms. Stage 6 is not a large-language-model certification or a guarantee of reliability on every task.\n\nThese stages are not a timeline of inventions. The Transformer paper appeared in 2017. Related breakthroughs appearing earlier in this game belong to its existing fictional setting, not public news from 2016. Heat maps and the “words of interest” in character reports are teaching and presentation devices, not measurements of the built-in local language model's internal attention.\n\nCurrent experience: Stage 3 may produce words or short fragments, rather than strictly one word." : "第一阶段：简单判断——从“是”与“否”开始\n\n它根据有限的线索作出简单判断。玩家通过提供示例与纠正答案，建立最初的教学关系，也开始发现：某些问题并不是靠一条简单规则就能分清的。\n\n第二阶段：组合特征——把几条线索放在一起看\n\n它开始综合多个特征作判断，处理更复杂的分类问题。玩家需要考虑的不只是数据数量，还有哪些线索有用、这些线索怎样共同影响答案。\n\n第三阶段：走向专长——学习看图与处理文字\n\n视觉和语言任务逐渐展开，它开始利用手写数字等已有数据，并接触验证码、图像与文字序列相关任务，从简单选择走向词语输出。不同任务需要不同的处理方式，“一套方法解决所有问题”开始遇到困难。\n\n第四阶段：保留信息——让前面的内容影响后面的回答\n\n它开始处理更长的信息，并尝试用短句交流。玩家能够感受到，它不再只对眼前一个词作反应，而是开始利用近期对话中的前文。说出一个词，逐渐变成接住你的一句话。近期保存的聊天内容可以跨天或读档后继续作为上下文；这与第五阶段从长期记录中检索相关信息的能力不同。\n\n第五阶段：寻找重点——从更多信息中找到相关线索\n\n面对更长的句子和更多记录，它需要找到与当前问题有关的内容。翻译、跨时间的交流等能力逐步展开，玩家也开始观察：它是否找对了依据，而不只是有没有给出一个流畅的回答。\n\n第六阶段：重构学习方式——走向更广泛的任务\n\n以 Transformer 等思路为灵感，游戏进入新的架构与规模发展阶段。它能够尝试更丰富的语言任务，但能力增长也带来新的问题：它在哪些地方可靠，哪些地方仍会出错，又是否适合交给别人使用？\n\n衔接整体意义：\n\n前四个阶段，我们更关心“它能不能学会”；到了后两个阶段，问题逐渐变成“它会成为什么”。能够交流是成长中的重要时刻，而如何理解、验证并对待它的能力，才是后半段想留给玩家的思考。\n\n阅读边界：第五阶段的注意力与长期记忆不是同一个机制；第六阶段也不是“大语言模型认证”或所有任务可靠的保证。\n\n六阶段不是技术发明时间线。Transformer 论文发表于 2017 年；游戏中提前出现的相关突破属于已有架空设定，不是 2016 年公开新闻。热力图与角色报告中的“关注词”是教学与表现设计，不是对内置本地语言模型内部注意力的实测。\n\n当前体验边界：第三阶段可能输出词语或短片段，并非严格只输出单个词。";
        public static string Title5(bool english) => english ? "How are real models trained, and who does the work?" : "真实模型怎样训练，训练人员怎样工作？";
        public static string Body5(bool english) => english ? "From data to a usable model\n\n1. Prepare data. Obtain appropriate permission to use it, collect, clean and deduplicate it, handle low-quality and private content, and keep training and evaluation data separate. A tokenizer converts text into tokens; one token does not always equal one Chinese character.\n\n2. Pretrain. For common autoregressive generative language models, the main task is predicting the next token from earlier ones. Across many examples, the model learns language patterns, knowledge associations and processing patterns useful in other tasks.\n\n3. Post-train. Use high-quality instruction-and-answer examples for supervised fine-tuning, and methods such as preference comparisons to adjust response tendencies. Further training may target mathematics, code or tool use. Models do not all use identical methods or sequences.\n\n4. Evaluate independently. Test questions and situations not directly used in training. Examine correctness, hallucinations, reliability, speed and regressions in capabilities.\n\n5. Deploy. Choose a version and apply runtime optimization or quantization as needed so users can access it. Deployment does not mean training continues with every conversation.\n\nA common training update\n\nInput a batch → forward computation → compute loss → backpropagate to obtain gradients → update parameters with an optimizer → continue with the next batch.\n\nParameter changes are distributed through the model; each question does not have its own neat knowledge cell. Lower training error does not guarantee improvement on every real task, so independent evaluation is still needed.\n\nTraining a model is not one person sitting and chatting with an AI all day. Large models usually involve several kinds of work:\n\nData engineering: clean, deduplicate and filter data, and maintain reproducible processing pipelines.\n\nAnnotation and domain expertise: write examples, correct errors, compare candidate answers and provide expert judgment.\n\nAlgorithms and training engineering: design methods, adjust configurations and analyze training logs and experiments.\n\nInfrastructure and distributed systems: manage multi-GPU computation, communication, storage, failures and recovery.\n\nEvaluation: design tests, find failure cases and assess readiness for release.\n\nDaily work often involves forming a hypothesis, running a small experiment, analyzing it, revising the plan and then scaling up. Human conversations and ratings can help produce data, but they must connect to a training process to cause parameter updates.\n\nGPU resources\n\nFor a model of about 2 billion parameters, 16-bit weights alone are about 4 GB at two bytes per parameter. Full-parameter training also stores gradients, optimizer states and intermediate results, potentially requiring tens of GB or more depending on the method, batch size and text length; multiple GPUs can share computation, the model or training states. Small-model training and methods that train only a subset of parameters, such as LoRA, may fit on one consumer GPU, so the two kinds of requirement should be considered separately. The model built into this game is Qwen3.5-2B fine-tuned with LoRA, running locally on your computer.\n\nThese memory figures explain training costs. They are not verified minimum or recommended requirements for this game. Running a quantized model for inference has different resource needs from training it." : "从数据到可使用的模型：\n\n1. 准备数据。取得适当使用权限，收集、清洗与去重资料，处理低质量和隐私内容，隔离训练与评估数据。用分词器将文本转换为 token；token 不固定等于一个汉字。\n2. 预训练。对常见的自回归生成式语言模型，主要任务是根据前文预测下一个 token。模型在大量样本中逐步学到语言规律、知识关联和可用于其他任务的处理模式。\n3. 后训练。使用优质指令回答示例进行监督微调；用偏好比较等方法调整回答倾向；也可以针对数学、代码、工具使用继续训练。并非每个模型都使用完全相同的方法与顺序。\n4. 独立评估。检查没直接参与训练的题目与场景，观察正确性、幻觉、可靠性、速度及能力退步等问题。\n5. 部署使用。选定版本，进行运行优化或量化等处理，让用户调用。部署不等于仍在随每次聊天持续训练。\n\n一次常见训练更新：输入一批数据 → 前向计算 → 计算损失 → 反向传播得到梯度 → 优化器更新参数 → 继续下一批数据。\n\n参数变化分布在模型中，不是一道题对应一个明确的知识格子。训练误差降低，不保证所有真实任务都改善，因此还要独立评估。\n\n“模型训练师”不是一个人坐着不断和 AI 聊天。大型模型通常由多类岗位协作：\n\n数据工程：清洗、去重、过滤，维护可重复的数据处理流程\n标注与领域专家：写示例、纠错、比较候选回答，提供专业判断\n算法与训练工程：设计方法、调节配置、分析训练日志和实验结果\n基础设施与分布式系统：处理多卡计算、通信、存储、故障与恢复\n评估：设计测试、寻找失败场景，确认是否适合发布\n\n日常工作往往是提出假设、做小规模实验、分析结果、修改方案，再扩大训练。人工聊天和评分可以参与数据生产，但必须接上训练流程，才会造成模型参数更新。\n\n补充显卡说明：以约 20 亿参数的模型为例，单是 16 位权重就约 4GB（每个参数 2 字节）。全参数训练还要存梯度、优化器状态和中间结果，可能需要数十 GB 或更多，具体取决于方法、批量大小与文本长度；多卡用于分担计算、模型或训练状态。小模型训练和 LoRA 这类只训练部分参数的微调，则可能在单张消费级显卡上完成，两者的资源需求要分开看。本作内置的模型就是用 LoRA 微调过的 Qwen3.5-2B，在你的电脑上本地运行。\n\n这里的显存数字用于解释训练开销，不是本作已经验证的最低或推荐运行配置。运行量化模型进行推理，与训练该模型的资源需求不同。";
        public static string Title6(bool english) => english ? "Why are context and memory different from training?" : "为什么上下文和记忆不等于训练？";
        public static string Body6(bool english) => english ? "Ordinary chat mainly uses forward computation: read the user's question and available context, then generate a reply with the current parameters. It usually does not compute training loss, backpropagate or update parameters with each conversation.\n\nYou just said your cat is called Tuantuan, and it answers correctly.\nPossible mechanism: reading the current chat context. Evidence of parameter training? No.\n\nIt remembers the name the next day.\nPossible mechanism: software saves a memory, then retrieves it or supplies it to the model. Evidence of parameter training? No.\n\nIt accepts a correction and uses the new answer in this conversation.\nPossible mechanism: adapting within the context. Evidence of parameter training? Usually not.\n\nConversations and ratings are processed into training data and an actual fine-tuning run occurs.\nMechanism: updating weights or trainable adapters. Evidence of training? Yes.\n\nIt would therefore be too absolute to say that conversations can never be used for training. With suitable authorization, selection and processing, conversations can support later training. Online learning systems can also be designed deliberately. Saving records, collecting feedback and completing training are three different states.\n\nThere are practical reasons not to write every sentence directly into parameters: inputs may be wrong or malicious; one person's preferences should not directly affect everyone; updates may damage existing capabilities; and privacy, cost and validation matter. A model saying “I learned it” is not proof that training occurred.\n\nIn this game, the built-in local language model is already trained when you start. Early yes/no behavior is a restriction imposed by the game's growth rules. It does not mean the model file on disk originally had only that capability. Your actions can genuinely change game state, available records, skill configuration and story events, but there is currently no basis for claiming that they retrain the built-in model's weights in real time." : "普通聊天主要是前向计算：读取用户问题和可用上下文，用当前参数生成回复。通常没有随每次聊天进行训练损失计算、反向传播与参数更新。\n\n刚说过猫叫团团，随后它回答正确\n可能机制：读取当前聊天上下文。是否说明参数被训练：否。\n\n第二天仍记得名字\n可能机制：软件保存记忆，再检索或提供给模型。是否说明参数被训练：否。\n\n接受纠正后，这轮对话改用新答案\n可能机制：上下文中的适应。是否说明参数被训练：通常不是。\n\n将对话和评价处理为训练数据，实际运行微调\n可能机制：更新权重或可训练适配器。是否说明参数被训练：是。\n\n\n因此不能绝对地说“聊天永远不能训练”。对话可以在适当授权、筛选和处理后用于后续训练，也可以专门设计在线学习系统。但保存记录、收集反馈、完成训练，是三个不同状态。\n\n不把每句话直接写进参数，有实际原因：用户输入可能错误或恶意，个人偏好不应直接影响所有人，更新可能损害已有能力，还需要考虑隐私、成本和验证。模型回复“我学会了”，不能作为训练完成的证据。\n\n对本作的解释：内置本地语言模型 从游戏开始就是已训练好的语言模型。角色初期只有“是/否”等表现，是游戏成长规则的限制，不代表磁盘上的模型文件原本只有该能力。玩家的行动可以真实改变游戏状态、可用记录、技能配置和剧情，但当前没有依据称它们在实时重训内置模型权重。";
    }
}
